<title>Nonvariceal Upper Gastrointestinal Bleeding: Management.</title>
<graphic href="eee0839-w0001.gif" />
<cell type="start" id="cell-1">
<label>Suspected upper GI bleeding (hematemesis or blood&#x002F;coffee grounds in NG aspiration). Initial clinical assessment, initial resuscitation and stabilization, assessment of mortality risk.</label>
<path target="cell-3">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-2">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-2">
<label>Assess risk of rebleeding.</label>
<path target="cell-4">High risk</path>
<path target="cell-5">Low risk</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-3">
<label>See &#x201C;GI bleed (variceal),&#x201D; <xref ref="fig001" />.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-4">
<label>ICU admission urgent&#x002F;emergent endoscopy.</label>
<path target="cell-6"></path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-5">
<label>Ward admission or hold in ER.</label>
<path target="cell-6"></path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-6">
<label>Endoscopy.</label>
<path target="cell-7">Esophageal or gastric varices</path>
<path target="cell-8">Ulcer</path>
<path target="cell-9">Erosive esophagitis</path>
<path target="cell-10">AVM</path>
<path target="cell-11">No source found</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-7">
<label>See &#x201C;GI bleed (variceal),&#x201D; <xref ref="fig001" />.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-8">
<label>Electrocautery or injection therapy and IV proton pump inhibitors. Successful?</label>
<path target="cell-12">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-13">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-12">
<label>Oral proton pump inhibitor, HP eradication, and close follow-up.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-13">
<label>Consider surgery or transcatheter embolization.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-9">
<label>IV proton pump inhibitors, test for HP, and close follow-up.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-10">
<label>Electrocautery or injection therapy.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-11">
<label>Colonoscopy and consider further diagnostic studies (angiography or tagged RBC scan).</label>
</cell>
<footnotes>
<footnote>Abbreviations: AVM, arteriovenous malformation; HP, <em>Helicobacter pylori</em>; NG, nastogastric.</footnote>
<footnote>
<sup>a</sup>Data from<xref ref="rule149" resource="acc002" />
</footnote>
</footnotes>
